The MIT licence above covers the source code only.

`lamellyx/data/` IS NOT DISTRIBUTED WITH THIS PACKAGE. It is listed in
.gitignore and excluded from the built wheel. Recreate it locally from a
CHARMM-GUI directory you already have:

    python -m lamellyx setup <gromacs_dir>

The reason is below. Neither the CHARMM-GUI licence nor the MacKerell lab's
force-field page states terms permitting redistribution; CHARMM-GUI's licence
says only that it is "free for academic and governmental use, but not for
commercial use". Absence of a stated permission is not permission, so the
files are not shipped.

What `data/` holds, once you have generated it:

  toppar/*.itp        CHARMM36 force-field parameters for POPC, TIP3P, K+ and
                      Cl-, in the GROMACS format produced by CHARMM-GUI's
                      force-field converter. The CHARMM36 parameters are the
                      work of the MacKerell laboratory and are distributed
                      under their own terms.

  POPC_conformers.npz Coordinates of 293 POPC molecules taken from an
  TIP3_cube.npz       equilibrated CHARMM36 bilayer, and a cube of equilibrated
                      TIP3P water. Coordinates only -- no parameters.

Checked 2026-08-10: https://mackerell.umaryland.edu/charmm_ff.shtml states no
licence, and https://www.charmm-gui.org/?doc=license_cgui grants academic and
governmental use without addressing redistribution of generated output. If
either of those changes, or if you obtain permission, `data/` can simply be
committed -- nothing in the code depends on its absence.

You may also skip `data/toppar/` entirely and point the `toppar` setting at
your own copy of the parameters; everything else keeps working.
